Optidy reviews the photos and videos a user permits on their device. It identifies exact duplicate photos, visually similar photos, possibly blurry photos, screenshots, Live Photos, large videos and edited videos. It can create a still copy of a Live Photo and a smaller 1080p or 720p video copy. It can also analyze an iPhone Storage screenshot and a user-selected Files folder on the device.

Optidy does not automatically delete photos or videos. The user chooses what to remove and confirms deletion through iOS. Photo, video, screenshot and selected-folder analysis runs on the device; Optidy does not upload those files to an ODA server.

Optidy Plus is an optional auto-renewable monthly or yearly subscription sold by Apple. Free users receive a small included allowance and may choose to watch rewarded ads for additional uses. Ads use Google Mobile Ads and Google User Messaging Platform. Optidy requests personalized ads only when the user’s consent choices allow them and iOS tracking permission is authorized. Otherwise, it requests only non-personalized ads. When tracking permission is still undecided, Optidy first asks during first launch after Google’s consent flow; if iOS cannot show the prompt then, Optidy tries again the first time the user taps Watch an ad.
